    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-03--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.58";
    dc:description "The learning assay and the blind and innervated controls map onto choice rates that the 2013 and 2017 papers publish for this Xenopus preparation. Those measurements cover the stated scope and can be checked for whether tail-eye animals outperform eyeless controls. Without deposited trial logs, a new analyst cannot recompute the statistics from raw choices.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: In the light-mediated learning assay, compare choice performance of tadpoles with ectopic tail eyes and native eyes removed against blind and normal-eyed animals; visual learning holds if only animals with a functional eye-brain path exceed chance.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Both positive reports come from the same group, so an independent replicate is not in the open record.", "Trial-level choice logs are in the papers' summaries, not a public repository.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.68"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.583"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
